 morate the 50th anniversary of the Apollo&#160\;11 moon landing\, the wor
 k combines string quartet music with Native stories about the moon\, illu
 minating&#160\;the rich storytelling traditions that have been passed thr
 ough generations of Indigenous communities.  &#160\;  A unique aspect of 
 this presentation is the participation of narrator Mike Pace\, a Lenape e
 ducator and former cultural interpreter at Conner Prairie.&#160\; Mike br
 ings a deeply personal perspective to the stories through his connections
  to Indiana's Native history\, including family ties to Chief Anderson\, 
 for whom the city of Anderson is named\, and to the Conner family associa
 ted with Conner Prairie.&#160\; His narration provides audiences with an 
 authentic and engaging&#160\;connection to the cultural themes explored t
 hroughout the program.For more information\, view this event in BeInvolve
 d (https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12843556).
